  "description": "Decode reject vectors (Phase 310). Each vector is a SHAPE, a JSON `input` (text, which may not parse), and the outcome computed by reading the input through the reference decoder of that shape: a `refusal` names the decode code (the closed DecodeCode set: InvalidJson, MissingField, WrongKind, UnknownTag, OutOfRange, UndeclaredMember, LimitExceeded, NotAdmitted, SchemaFault) and the path, as an array of member keys (strings) and item indices (integers) from the document root; `accepted` marks an input the shape reads. Shapes: string | int | float | bool | any; list (of, optional maxItems: more items is LimitExceeded at the array); object (fields of name, shape, optional; optional closed: an undeclared member is UndeclaredMember at that member); tagged (key, cases of tag and shape, the case shape reading the SAME object; an absent or non-string tag is refused at the key, an unknown one is UnknownTag there, and a tag outside an optional admit list is NotAdmitted there); intRange (min, max: outside is OutOfRange); ref (name, resolved against the vector's definitions: unresolved is SchemaFault). An object's fields are read in order and the first refusal is the answer; an absent optional field is accepted and a present ill-typed one refused. A MissingField path names the absent member. A vector without a `limits` member is parsed at the parser's own cap of 512 nested containers and no other bound. A vector WITH one (Phase 465) is parsed under that record — `depth` (nested containers admitted), `stringLength` (Unicode code points in one string or member key, a surrogate pair counting as one), `arrayLength` (items in one array), `objectMembers` (members in one object), `documentBytes` (UTF-8 bytes of the whole input) — each enforced on the way down, before the container, unit, item or member it guards is read: a breach is LimitExceeded at the path of the container it was raised in (the string's own path for a string value, the object's for a key, the root for documentBytes) and is never InvalidJson; malformed text is InvalidJson exactly as without the record; and the first fault in document order wins. A host certifies its decode error contract by reproducing every code and path; the sentence beside a refusal is the host's own.",
